### FILE 1 — `notification-service/src/main/java/com/vivek/notification/listener/NotificationListener.java`

**Problem:** `throws Exception` on the listener method causes Spring Kafka to retry the message on any failure, including bad JSON. The catch block re-throws, making the `try/catch` pointless.

```java
package com.vivek.notification.listener;

import io.micrometer.core.instrument.MeterRegistry;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;

import org.springframework.kafka.annotation.KafkaListener;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonProcessingException;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import com.vivek.notification.dto.AssignmentEvent;

@Component
@Slf4j
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class NotificationListener {

    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper;
    private final MeterRegistry meterRegistry;

    @KafkaListener(topics = "ambulance-assigned-topic", groupId = "notification-group")
    public void consumeAssignment(String message) {
        // DO NOT declare `throws Exception` — Spring Kafka retries indefinitely on any thrown exception.
        // Malformed JSON must be caught and discarded here; KafkaDltConfig handles retryable errors.
        AssignmentEvent event;
        try {
            event = objectMapper.readValue(message, AssignmentEvent.class);
        } catch (JsonProcessingException e) {
            meterRegistry.counter("notification.assignments.parse_error.total").increment();
            log.error("Malformed assignment message in notification-service — discarding (goes to DLT): {}", message, e);
            return; // discard — do not rethrow
        }

        try {
            sendNotification(event);
            meterRegistry.counter("notification.assignments.consumed.total").increment();
            meterRegistry.counter("notification.sent.total").increment();
            log.info("Notification dispatched emergencyId={} ambulanceId={} distanceKm={} version={}",
                    event.getEmergencyId(), event.getAmbulanceId(),
                    event.getDistanceKm(), event.getVersion());
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Rethrow only for genuinely retryable errors (e.g. downstream SMS/push service failure).
            // KafkaDltConfig will retry 3 times with 2s backoff, then send to DLT.
            meterRegistry.counter("notification.consume.failures.total").increment();
            log.error("Failed to send notification emergencyId={} — will retry via KafkaDltConfig",
                    event.getEmergencyId(), e);
            throw new RuntimeException("Notification send failed, triggering retry", e);
        }
    }

    /**
     * Notification dispatch stub.
     * Replace with real SMS/push/webhook logic in production.
     * Throwing here intentionally triggers Kafka retry (unlike parse errors above).
     */
    private void sendNotification(AssignmentEvent event) {
        // TODO: integrate with Twilio / FCM / webhook
        log.info("[STUB] Would send SMS/push to caller: emergencyId={} ambulanceId={} eta={}km",
                event.getEmergencyId(), event.getAmbulanceId(), event.getDistanceKm());
    }
}
